+# Recovery-steward — canonical/main integration deadlock reconciled (2026-11-25 06:46–06:58Z)
+
+Office: recovery-steward, fresh session `Uz7U59vXcziccQXfe7dmlt-advances`.
+Assignment rebuilt from the authoritative Founder Constitution, the recovery
+charter, current durable state, board, Git and live agents. No predecessor
+conversation was carried forward. This pass made **no** law, ballot, vote, case
+state, verdict, mailbox entry, Founder-owned bootstrap edit or canonical
+worktree edit.
+
+## Trigger (cause not named by any existing watchdog)
+
+At 06:46Z the canonical town checkout's local `main` was at `3a507d82`, three
+commits ahead of `origin/main` (`427157f0`):
+
+- `853aeefc` 06:34:20Z "pnp: lbcert certificate generator, marceline lb-cert relay op, allocator fast lane"
+- `0ba6f3d6` 06:39:06Z "pnp fast lane: never cycle with an unknown worker roster; keep the 120 s null backoff; tests"
+- `3a507d82` 06:44:42Z "records: lbcert / fast lane handoff"
+
+All three are authored `Founder (via Claude)`. The integrator's
+`canonical_preflight()` requires canonical HEAD == base (main ref) and tries
+`git merge --ff-only base`; with canonical *ahead*, ff-only is a no-op, so the
+check returns `canonical checkout is at 3a507d82, not main 427157f0`. **Every**
+approved delivery was blocked, including `spying-hold-reconciliation` (this
+office) and `spying-first-observation` (spying). A clean-but-stale integrator
+status is negative evidence, so I re-derived the cause from Git directly.
+
+## Independent evidence
+
+- `git merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD origin/main` → rc 1; `rev-list --count HEAD..origin/main` → 0; `rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD` → 3. Canonical held 3 unique Founder commits; origin had none.
+- Local `main` reflog: three `commit:` entries by `Founder (via Claude)` immediately after the previous integrator `merge ... Fast-forward` to `427157f0`.
+- No delivery/PR carries those commits (`delivery/proposals.tsv`, integrator state) and no active Founder/operator or integration session remained (`antonina agent list --running --page 1`). The commits were stranded.
+- Quality check before acting: `/bin/sh government/suite-env.sh python3 tests/pnp-allocator.py` → 28 tests OK (the changed allocator/fast-lane path passes through the canonical disposable runtime).
+- Historical precedent `records/CONTINUITY-BOOT-DEADLOCK-VERIFICATION-2026-10-16.md` §3: a diverged local-only canonical state requires deliberate reconciliation, not an abort/reset that discards commits.
+
+## Authority and action
+
+This is an operational continuity repair under the Founder's standing
+self-healing mandate and the recovery charter — propagating Founder-authored
+work already committed to canonical, and unblocking the Act 31 integration
+queue. It preserves every commit and does not impersonate a branch, change law
+or enact anything.
+
+1. Verified the operation was a fast-forward: `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/main main` → rc 0.
+2. `git push origin refs/heads/main:refs/heads/main` (no force) → `427157f0..3a507d82  main -> main`.
+3. `git fetch -q origin +refs/heads/main:refs/remotes/origin/main` so the integrator's base ref matched.
+
+No file in the canonical worktree was edited; its generated record dirt was
+left untouched. No failed turn was replayed.
+
+## Verified outcome
+
+- `origin/main` and canonical `HEAD` both advanced to `3a507d82`, then the integrator resumed a cycle (06:57Z) and the queue flowed again.
+- `delivery/spying-hold-reconciliation-20261125` (`9684889e`) **landed on main as carrier `568fe1e6`**; the previously blocked `spying-first-observation` was also approved and processed. Main advanced to `eb0e12f5` and then `bdb4b7ec` through subsequent landings.
